  "dom_id": "step-q357007",
  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "Let $p=-6$ and $q=9.$ What point on the number line corresponds to $p+q?$",
  "worked_solution": "The value of $p+q$ is the number located a distance $|q|$ from $p$ on the number line, \n\n- moving to the *right* if $q$ is *positive*, and\n\n- moving to the *left* if $q$ is *negative*.\n\nIn our situation:\n\n- We start at $p=-6$ on the number line.\n\n- Here, $q=9$, so the distance we move is $|q|=9.$\n\n- Because $q$ is *positive*, we move $9$ units to the *right* from $-6.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14152428/assets/17c56561e34f16a80df8ee8872401f7a3df4930c28c38ce70c1dcf202269f3d0.png)\n\nThis point corresponds to the number\n\n$$\n-6+9=3.\n$$",
